Origin of adhesion in humid air — Kim and colleagues (@cm-humidity-source: 0, is #reference, #part-of @cm-sources) { r_5KY9XHR2M0AZYYGJRNTFPCPB0H
Doo-In Kim, Jaroslaw Grobelny, Pradeep N. Namboodiri and Robert F. Cook. *Origin of Adhesion in Humid Air*, Langmuir 24 (2008). [NIST catalogue, dated 18 April 2008](https://www.nist.gov/publications/origin-adhesion-humid-air) · [Institutional full-text link](https://tsapps.nist.gov/publication/get_pdf.cfm?pub_id=851021).

The authors compare nanoscale pull-off measurements over controlled environments and interpret them using a model that combines contact deformation and meniscus effects. Study the actual apparatus, calibration, surface conditions and inference before transferring its result to a manufacturing process.

Only the official metadata and abstract were inspected on 30 October 2026. The browser could not open the PDF and local retrieval returned HTTP 403. No figure, numerical result or reuse licence is claimed verified. The abstract supplies a research question here; full-paper comparison remains reading work for the learner when the institutional text is accessible.

